    <string name="dlg_internal_title">Use internal storage?</string>
    <string name="dlg_internal_msg">A dashcam writes continuously — as long as it is recording, it is writing.\n\nFlash memory has a limited write endurance. Using the head unit's internal storage as the dashcam's destination will measurably consume that endurance, and this storage usually cannot be replaced.\n\nA USB drive is recommended: it can be swapped when it wears out, and pulled out to copy files off.</string>
